    "body": "## What\n\nKeep a bounded live output tail on background bash cards, show elapsed and last-output timing, add `/jobs follow <job-id>` with a read-only scrollable output pane, and make collapsed bash preview height configurable. Integrated the current fork without replacing its newer shared render helpers or command-submission handling.\n\n## Why\n\nLong-running commands should remain visibly active after automatic backgrounding so progress and quiet periods are distinguishable.\n\n## Testing\n\nBefore integration: 49 focused tests passed (187 assertions), and an actual tmux TUI scenario exercised background updates after the agent turn, quiet timing, preview-height changes, transcript rebuilding, follow pause/resume/close, and failed exits. On current head `70367c97`: local workspace lint/format/type checks passed, a real TUI smoke exercised bounded live output, quiet timing, late output, and exit status, and the native tool-description smoke verified background timing, follow hints, and the configured tail height. Exact-head Woodpecker pipeline #113 passed TypeScript and Rust checks, the web build, the PipeWire-enabled native build, CLI compilation, and the fork-version equality check. Fork CI intentionally disables test suites. No local native/shipping build or installation.\n\nSigned Arch delivery verified: merged-source pipeline #116 passed, and package pipeline #216 built source `dc016552309da58678910b5bd6970e4ba7145624` with recipe `8a6eb2b8b4d1b82d34ac94b26c36e5d46cff8cd2`. `vith-arch` publishes `oh-my-pi-vith-git 18.4.8.vith.r333.gdc016552309d-1`; both database and package signatures verify against the fully trusted repository key. The downloaded package SHA-256 matches the signed database (`4fdc615365138c749ca05542c19e2ec253cd3c7ed7c4b3775b60d54a406ad797`), and the extracted published binary prints `omp/18.4.8+vith-fork.333.dc016552309d`. No installation or local native/shipping build was performed.\n\n---\n\n- [x] `bun check` passes\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [ ] CHANGELOG updated with the required attribution (if user-facing; internal issue fixes use issue links, external contributions add the PR link and contributor credit after creation)\n\nChangelog intentionally unchanged because no changelog update was requested. Signed Arch publication is verified; installation is left to the user.\n",
